s=Slide('Current architecture: browser → adapter → API → data','A same-origin website adapter bridges a body-authenticated backend API','Website/server/app.mjs, api.mjs, render.yaml; Backend/Program.cs, Sql.cs, Env.cs, Listing.cs','The browser calls the Node website origin for static assets and /api routes. Node translates body credentials and GET bodies, retains opaque-cookie session mappings and a service admin token in memory, and uses HTTPS to the configured ASP.NET service. Shared helpers read the configured SQLite account database. ListingController bypasses the shared Sql helper and independently uses ../Data.db. The team confirms the backend is deployed on Azure and the website at https://studentexchange.onrender.com. This review does not independently establish the deployed source revision or current full workflow acceptance. There is no third-party OAuth, payment or messaging service integration in the source.',takeaway='The adapter is necessary for both protocol compatibility and keeping shared/user credentials out of the browser.')
