s=Slide('UML class view: shared credentials and request inheritance','These are actual C# request types, not invented service/entity classes','Backend/Components/AppAuthJson.cs; Controllers/Register.cs, LogIn.cs, Admin.cs','Explain that AppAuthJson combines body fields with static validation operations in the current code. Register.Info, LogIn.Info and Admin.Info inherit those fields. Nullable request properties support per-operation handling; they do not mean that required registration/login fields are optional at runtime. These DTOs differ from the database tables and from Node’s browser-safe TypeScript contracts. The schema model follows on separate slides. This design also exposes a coupling trade-off: validation and request shape share a class.',takeaway='The inherited access_token is the acting user token; admin_token is a separate service forwarding token.')
