s=Slide('UML sequence: login establishes a website session','Prepared forwarding identity is assumed; its renewal rules are covered in the appendix','docs/uml D10; api.mjs /api/login; LogIn.Post; Register.Get','Time flows downward. Backend login verifies credentials/attempt admission, reuses or issues a token and returns it only to Node. Node then uses GET /Register with the token in the JSON body to obtain a public profile. Only a validated profile permits local session creation. The browser receives a projected profile and opaque HttpOnly cookie, not the backend token. The Node self-message denotes the local Map write. Backend token validity and local session validity are separate clocks. Failed login/profile read is an alternative result; it does not establish the new Map entry.',takeaway='A backend login response alone is insufficient; profile projection succeeds before Node creates the browser session.')
