s=Slide('Database core: one school, many users, optional admin membership','UML-style relational model of four declared tables; these are not ORM entity classes','DB_Schema.txt; Register.cs; LogIn.cs; Components/Sql.cs','The declared account core includes Schools, User, Admins and Access_Token. User.school_id is required; an account can have zero or one Admins row and many access tokens. Email/token uniqueness matters to lookup and issuance. The schema declares RESTRICT for school/user and user/admin relationships and CASCADE for tokens, but the connection does not explicitly enable foreign keys. Do not claim these runtime effects were verified. Password and email values are deterministically reversibly encrypted in the current code, which is a security debt rather than a recommended password strategy.',takeaway='Declared constraints explain intended relationships; actual foreign-key enforcement still needs a runtime check.')
