s=Slide('Security data: attempts are observations, not always blocks','Four more declared tables track IP identity, user/IP association and attempt windows','DB_Schema.txt; Users.cs; IP.cs; docs/dfd P35/P43/P44','These complete the eight-table declared schema. Multiple historical attempt rows may exist, so draw 0..* rather than assuming a unique per-user row. User_Has_IPs has NOT NULL foreign keys and a unique pair. The active time window and count determine blocking, not merely table membership. A successful first observation can have count -1. At user threshold 10, existing tokens are revoked; clearing attempts later does not recreate them. IP blocks do not directly revoke tokens. Process-local identity locks serialize related updates but do not coordinate multiple instances.',takeaway='Token records, attempt windows and process-local lock metadata have different purposes and retention rules.')
