s=Slide('Major implementation risks: next integration priorities','Severity and proposed accountable roles are review recommendations, not completed fixes','Listing.cs; DB_Schema.txt; DeterministicEncryption.cs; Sql.cs; api.mjs; team role report','Lead with the risks that could prevent a correct final demo. ListingController accepts UserId and delete ID without shared auth or ownership and uses an undeclared table on a separately resolved database path. Passwords are reversibly encrypted instead of stored with a dedicated salted password hash. The live service-token migration is unverified. These are implementation findings, not theoretical checklists. Proposed remediation ownership follows the user-supplied roles; it is not a claim that those tasks are already in progress. A class-project demonstration must still avoid presenting unauthenticated destructive listing operations as correct ownership behavior.',takeaway='Prioritize coherent persistence, authenticated ownership and current deployed workflow acceptance.')
