s=Slide('Two concrete quality issues found during this review','Fresh checks reveal actionable defects without rewriting the application during presentation work','src/App.test.tsx:20; App.tsx listing-grid and offer input; evidence files','Issue one: the test expects getByRole(list, name Sample listings), but the current ul.listing-grid has no accessible label. The fix should restore the intended accessible name, keeping a meaningful assertion, not simply deleting the test. Issue two: min=0.01 with step=1 makes $20.00 a native step mismatch; $20.01 succeeds and produces a local preview. Proposed fix: choose cent precision, positive validation and a browser test for whole-dollar and fractional values. These observations are separate from the 116 passed count. Both fixes belong in application work after this review; they were not silently applied to change the evidence.',takeaway='Use the failing accessibility expectation and whole-dollar offer case as focused regression acceptance tests.')
s.card(65,215,715,420,'Accessible catalog name','Observed: 1 App test fails because “Sample listings” is no longer an accessible list name. Proposed fix: restore the intended label and retain a behavior-focused test. Owner proposal: Andrew + frontend team.',RED)
s.card(820,215,715,420,'Offer amount validity','Observed: min=0.01 with step=1 rejects $20.00; $20.01 succeeds. Proposed fix: step=0.01, positive-value checks and a browser-level amount regression. Owner proposal: Robert Richardson + Andrew.',GOLD)
