s=Slide('Appendix | route and permission reference','Browser routes translate into current backend body contracts','Website/server/api.mjs, admin.mjs; Backend controllers and AppAuthJson','Use when asked a precise API question. Shared app and service forwarding fields are supplied by Node. Public Schools GET is parameterless in the backend even when the adapter sends a body. Token-protected GET bodies require Node transport. Admin profile/deletion use caller token and to_user; blocked selectors email/IP are separate from to_user. Backend directory level visibility begins at 27 but the UI projection uses 30. Admin DELETE logout can mask validation failure. This table is selective; the complete source/DFD route register is linked in the evidence README.',section='APPENDIX · TECHNICAL DETAIL')
s.table(['Browser contract','Backend operation','Permission / detail'],[['POST /api/register; /api/login','POST /Register; POST /LogIn + GET /Register','Register does not log in; Node creates cookie only after profile.'],['GET/PATCH /api/profile','GET/PATCH /Register','Valid session/user token; PATCH has separate readback.'],['POST /api/logout','DELETE /LogIn','Idempotent/qualified confirmation; local cleanup.'],['GET/DELETE /api/admin/users','GET /Users; DELETE /Register','Admin ≥ 10; deletion requires to_user.'],['GET/PATCH /api/admin/profile','GET/PATCH /Register with to_user','Admin ≥ 10 + lower-rank/locked-target guards.'],['GET/DELETE /api/admin/blocked','GET/DELETE /Blocked','Admin ≥ 20; email XOR ip_addr for clearing.'],['POST/PATCH/DELETE /api/admin','Same verbs /Admin','Admin > 0; assigned level below caller; locked requires 30.'],['GET/POST/DELETE /api/admin/schools','Same verbs /Schools','Admin ≥ 10 for website management.']],[490,470,510],top=198,rowh=67,size=17)

s=Slide('Appendix | three edge cases that reveal design understanding','Protocol adaptation, saved writes and qualified revocation each require distinct handling','api.mjs upstream/forwarding/profile/logout; AppAuthJson.cs; LogIn.cs','Explain three non-obvious cases. Forwarding token expiry is explicitly recognized as pre-operation rejection and permits a single coalesced service-token renewal/retry; ordinary server, forbidden or visitor-expired errors do not permit replay. A committed profile write followed by a failed read returns saved status with profile null and should not silently repeat a password update. Logout returns success even on certain backend token-validation failures; the UI must not certify target revocation. These are precisely the sort of details that show the team understands its implementation, beyond the names of frameworks.',section='APPENDIX · TECHNICAL DETAIL',takeaway='Different failure semantics must produce different client behavior; “retry everything” is incorrect.')
s.card(65,218,470,430,'Forwarding token expired','A marked backend rejection precedes the operation. Renew the service login once; share concurrent refresh; preserve visitor token and request fields. Do not replay arbitrary errors.',BLUE)
